{title: Lord, Enthroned in Heavenly Splendor}
{artist: George H. Bourne / William Owen}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Response}
{key: Am}
{key_original: Gm}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 6/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Lord_Enthroned_In_Heavenly_Splendor-Bryn_Calfaria)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Lord, enthroned [E]in [Am]heav’nly splen[E]dor,
[Am]First begott[Dm]en [E]from the dead,
[Am]You alone, [E]our [Am]strong defend[E]er,
[Am]Now lift up [Dm]Your [E]people’s head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Alleluia! [E]Alle[Dm]lu[E]ia! [Am]Al[G]le[C]luia!
[Dm]Je[G]sus, [C]true [F]and li[Dm]ving [E]bread!
[E]Jesus, [Am]true [Dm]and li[E]ving [Am]bread!
{end_of_chorus}
